# Butler Routes - Ironforge completionist (pack butler-routes-completionist, v1).
# Every Ironforge City quest in the local census (188 quests,
# docs/ironforge-census.md) appears exactly once as an accept; every one is
# turned in once except 95924/95925, which have no turn-in in the data.
# Ironforge is a hub the character returns to across their whole
# leveling life, so the route is ordered for repeated use: grouped by district
# with chains kept together, then accept-based expeditions by destination zone.
# Quest levels run 1-60 (min-levels 1-60); high-level legs carry notes saying
# which level they belong to. Coordinates in Ironforge use the era frame;
# expedition stops use the frames their data carries, set with zone map lines.
guide butler-routes-completionist/ironforge-city
title Ironforge - Completionist
levels 1-60
zone Ironforge
faction Alliance
category Leveling
folder Cities
keywords ironforge, city, completionist
coords live
version 1

step Ironforge — arrival at the Gates

  note Ironforge is a hub for the whole leveling life: come in through the Gates, set your hearth at Innkeeper Firebrew in the west when you pass her, and learn the gryphon route at Gryth Thurden. Quests here span level 1 to 60 — the steps say which legs belong to which level; low-level arrivals do the early steps and come back for the rest.
  goto 51.52,26.31
  accept 6388 only Dwarf,Gnome -- Gryth Thurden - Golnir Bouldertoe takes it
  note 6388's pre (6391) lives in the Dun Morogh guide — take 6388 after that leg.
  goto 55.5,47.74
  turnin 6388 only Dwarf,Gnome -- Gryth Thurden - Golnir's word to Gryth Thurden
  accept 6392 only Dwarf,Gnome -- Return to Brock - Gryth Thurden; Brock Stoneseeker waits in Loch Modan
  note Brock's Loch Modan turn-in is an expedition below.

